There are several PHP libraries available that can be used to build an AI chatbot. Some of the popular ones include:
1. BotMan - BotMan is a PHP chatbot framework that allows developers to build chatbots for multiple messaging platforms such as Facebook Messenger, Slack, Telegram, and more. It provides a simple and intuitive API that makes it easy to build chatbots from scratch.
2. Wit.ai - Wit.ai is a natural language processing platform that can be used to build chatbots. It provides easy-to-use APIs for text and voice-based interactions, and supports multiple languages.
3. Dialogflow - Dialogflow is a Google-owned natural language processing platform that can be used to build chatbots. It provides a wide range of features such as speech recognition, intent recognition, and entity extraction.
4. ChatterBot - ChatterBot is a Python-based chatbot framework that can be used to build chatbots in PHP. It uses machine learning algorithms to generate responses to user queries.
Regarding whether to use a pre-existing framework or build the chatbot from scratch, it depends on your specific requirements and expertise. If you have experience in building chatbots and want more control over the chatbot's functionality, building from scratch may be a better option. On the other hand, if you want to save time and effort, using a pre-existing framework like BotMan can be a good choice.
Here's an example code snippet for building a simple chatbot using BotMan:
```
<?php
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
use BotMan\BotMan\BotMan;
use BotMan\BotMan\BotManFactory;
use BotMan\BotMan\Drivers\DriverManager;
$config = [
    'facebook' => [
        'token' => 'YOUR_FACEBOOK_TOKEN',
        'app_secret' => 'YOUR_FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET',
        'verification' => 'YOUR_FACEBOOK_VERIFICATION',
    ]
];
DriverManager::loadDriver(\BotMan\Drivers\Facebook\FacebookDriver::class);
$botman = BotManFactory::create($config);
$botman->hears('hello', function (BotMan $bot) {
    $bot->reply('Hello, how can I assist you today?');
});
$botman->hears('help', function (BotMan $bot) {
    $bot->reply('I can help you with anything from weather updates to restaurant recommendations. Just ask!');
});
$botman->hears('weather in {city}', function (BotMan $bot, $city) {
    // Code to fetch weather data for the given city
    $weather_data = get_weather_data($city);
    $bot->reply('The current temperature in ' . $city . ' is ' . $weather_data['temperature'] . ' degrees Celsius.');
});
$botman->listen();
```
This code sets up a simple chatbot that can respond to three different types of user queries: "hello", "help", and "weather in {city}". When the user types "hello" or "help", the bot responds with a pre-defined message. When the user types "weather in {city}", the bot fetches weather data for the given city and responds with the current temperature.

