double initialPopulation = 1000;
double growthRate = 100;
int years = 10;
for (int i = 1; i <= years; i++)
{
    double population = initialPopulation + growthRate * i;
    Console.WriteLine($"Population after {i} years: {population}");
}
```
In this example, we're using a simple linear function to calculate the population after a certain number of years, given an initial population and a growth rate. Note that the growth rate is much higher than in the previous example, to make the difference more apparent.
