Inside the loop, we calculate the current index as `i % arr.length`, which uses the modulo operator (%) to "wrap around" the index when it reaches the end of the array. For example, when `i` is 3, the index will be 0 (since 3 % 3 is 0), so we will start over at the beginning of the array.

