Another useful tool for debugging Go code is the "panic" and "recover" functions. These functions can help you handle unexpected errors and gracefully recover from them. To use the "panic" function, simply call it with an error message when an unexpected error occurs in your code. To recover from the error and continue running your program, use the "recover" function in a deferred function. Here is an example of how to use these functions:
func main() {
