}
```
This code uses the "github.com/kljensen/snowball" package to perform stemming, which is the process of reducing words to their base or root form. Stemming is a common preprocessing step in many NLP tasks, including text classification and information retrieval.
Alternative Python code for stemming:
```python
from nltk.stem import SnowballStemmer
text = "Natural language processing is the task of processing natural language."
stemmer = SnowballStemmer("english")
stemmed_text = " ".join([stemmer.stem(word) for word in text.split()])
print(stemmed_text)
```
This code uses the "nltk" library to perform stemming. The "SnowballStemmer" class is used to create a stemmer for the English language. The "stem" method is used to stem each word in the text, and the "join" method is used to join the stemmed words back into a single string.
Alternative Java code for stemming:
```java
import org.tartarus.snowball.ext.EnglishStemmer;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "Natural language processing is the task of processing natural language.";
        EnglishStemmer stemmer = new EnglishStemmer();
        StringBuilder stemmedText = new StringBuilder();
        for (String word : text.split(" ")) {
            stemmer.setCurrent(word);
            stemmer.stem();
            stemmedText.append(stemmer.getCurrent()).append(" ");
        }
        System.out.println(stemmedText.toString().trim());
    }
}
```
This code uses the "Snowball" library to perform stemming. The "EnglishStemmer" class is used to create a stemmer for the English language. The "setCurrent" method is used to set the word to be stemmed, and the "stem" method is used to perform stemming. The stemmed words are then appended to a StringBuilder and joined back into a single string.

