```csharp
using System;
class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Get user input
        Console.Write("Enter the principal: ");
        double principal = double.Parse(Console.ReadLine());
        Console.Write("Enter the annual interest rate (as a decimal): ");
        double interestRate = double.Parse(Console.ReadLine());
        Console.Write("Enter the number of times the interest is compounded per year: ");
        int compoundingPeriods = int.Parse(Console.ReadLine());
        Console.Write("Enter the number of years: ");
        int years = int.Parse(Console.ReadLine());
        Console.Write("Enter the amount of additional contributions made each year: ");
        double additionalContributions = double.Parse(Console.ReadLine());
        // Calculate the compound interest rate with additional contributions
        double compoundInterest = principal * Math.Pow(1 + (interestRate / compoundingPeriods), compoundingPeriods * years);
        double totalContributions = additionalContributions * years;
        double finalBalance = compoundInterest + totalContributions;
        // Display the results
        Console.WriteLine("The compound interest rate with additional contributions is: " + finalBalance.ToString("C"));
    }
}
```
This program prompts the user for the principal, interest rate, compounding periods, number of years, and additional contributions made each year. It then calculates the compound interest rate using the formula `P(1 + r/n)^(nt)` where `P` is the principal, `r` is the annual interest rate, `n` is the number of times the interest is compounded per year, and `t` is the number of years. It also calculates the total contributions made over the years and adds it to the final balance.
Finally, the program displays the result as a string formatted as currency using the `ToString("C")` method.

