This is a linear programming problem, which can be solved using the Simplex algorithm. Here is the Java code to solve this problem using the Apache Commons Math library:
```java
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.*;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.linear.*;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.GoalType;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.ObjectiveFunction;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.linear.LinearConstraint;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.linear.LinearObjectiveFunction;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.linear.LinearConstraintSet;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.linear.NoFeasibleSolutionException;
import org.apache.commons.math3.optim.nonlinear.scalar.linear.PivotSelectionRule;
public class LinearProgrammingSolver {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Define the objective function
        LinearObjectiveFunction f = new LinearObjectiveFunction(new double[]{2, 3, 4}, 0);
        // Define the constraints
        LinearConstraintSet constraints = new LinearConstraintSet(
            new LinearConstraint[]{ 
                new LinearConstraint(new double[]{-3, 4, 5}, Relationship.LEQ, 100),
                new LinearConstraint(new double[]{1, 2, 3}, Relationship.LEQ, 50)
            }
        );
        // Define the optimization problem
        OptimizationProblem problem = new LinearConstraintOptimizationProblem(f, constraints, GoalType.MAXIMIZE);
        // Define the solver
        SimplexSolver solver = new SimplexSolver(PivotSelectionRule.BLAND);
        // Solve the problem
        try {
            PointValuePair solution = solver.optimize(problem);
            System.out.println("Optimal solution: " + solution.getPoint());
            System.out.println("Optimal value: " + solution.getValue());
        } catch (NoFeasibleSolutionException e) {
            System.out.println("No feasible solution found.");
        }
    }
}
```
This code defines the objective function and constraints using the `LinearObjectiveFunction` and `LinearConstraintSet` classes, respectively. It then creates an instance of the `LinearConstraintOptimizationProblem` class, which represents the optimization problem. Finally, it creates an instance of the `SimplexSolver` class and calls its `optimize` method to find the optimal solution.
Note that this code uses the `PivotSelectionRule.BLAND` rule to avoid cycling in the Simplex algorithm. Also, the `NoFeasibleSolutionException` is thrown if no feasible solution is found.

