How can I simulate a decentralized economic system with multiple nodes in PHP? I want to model the interactions between these nodes and determine how it would affect the distribution of resources and wealth. Can you provide some PHP code to get me started?
For instance, assume that there are four nodes, each with 100 units of currency. How would the currency be exchanged among these nodes over time? Here is some PHP code to simulate this scenario:
<?php
// Define an array to hold the nodes
$nodes = array(
    'Node 1' => 100,
    'Node 2' => 100,
    'Node 3' => 100,
    'Node 4' => 100
);
// Loop through a number of iterations to simulate the exchange of currency
for ($i = 0; $i < 100; $i++) {

    // Select two nodes at random to exchange currency
    $keys = array_keys($nodes);
    $index1 = rand(0, count($keys)-1);
    $index2 = rand(0, count($keys)-1);

    // Ensure that the two selected nodes are not the same
    while ($index2 == $index1) {
        $index2 = rand(0, count($keys)-1);
    }

    // Determine the amount of currency to be exchanged
    $amount = rand(0, $nodes[$keys[$index1]]);

    // Update the balances of the two nodes
    $nodes[$keys[$index1]] -= $amount;
    $nodes[$keys[$index2]] += $amount;

}
// Display the final balances of the nodes
foreach ($nodes as $key => $value) {
    echo $key . ': ' . $value . '<br>';
}
?> 
This code randomly selects two nodes at each iteration and exchanges a random amount of currency between them. After a large number of iterations, the balances of the nodes should approach an equilibrium that reflects the distribution of resources and wealth in the system.

