```
function encrypt(sentence, key) {
  let encrypted = '';
  for (let i = 0; i < sentence.length; i++) {
    let charCode = sentence.charCodeAt(i);
    if (charCode >= 65 && charCode <= 90) { // uppercase letters
      charCode = ((charCode - 65) + key.length) % 26 + 65; // shift by key length
    } else if (charCode >= 97 && charCode <= 122) { // lowercase letters
      charCode = ((charCode - 97) + key.length) % 26 + 97; // shift by key length
    }
    encrypted += String.fromCharCode(charCode);
  }
  if (key === 'secret') {
    encrypted += ' *'; // add a marker if the key is 'secret'
  }
  return encrypted;
}
```
This algorithm works by iterating over each character in the sentence and performing a mathematical operation on its ASCII code. If the character is an uppercase or lowercase letter, it is shifted by the length of the key using modular arithmetic to wrap around the alphabet. The resulting encrypted message is then returned, along with a marker if the key is 'secret'.
