\section{Analysis of the outcome and impact}
The outcome of the Battle of Waterloo was a decisive victory for the coalition forces. Napoleon was exiled again, this time to the island of Saint Helena, and the Napoleonic Wars officially came to an end. The battle had a significant impact on European history, as it marked the end of the French Empire and the beginning of a new era of peace and stability in Europe.
